  "summary": "I graduated in May 2020 with a Bachelor's Degree in Computer Science from Georgia Tech. At Tech I specialized in Artificial Intelligence and Computational Theory. I have always had an engineer's passion for problem solving and building new things, so as I became more and more familiar with computers growing up, computer science/software engineering a great passion of mine.\n\nMost of my school work was in AI specifically Machine Learning and Computer Vision. In my own time though I taught myself Web Development and have since used that to work on a couple of projects.\n\nI consider myself a decent leader. In high school, I was the president of numerous clubs including the president of my school's Beta Club and the president and founder of my school's Competition Robotics Team. In my early years at college I worked as a part-time student teacher where I would help tutor other college students in Math and Computer Science, and later in college, I became president of a student organization as well as leading many class-based team projects.",
